Yes, this is exactly what we are going to do.
Dependency injection is the process of injecting an instance of a class into
another object. The goal of dependency injection is to decouple a class
from its dependencies so that the dependencies can be changed without
changing the class. ASP.NET Core has its own dependency injection
facility that allows class dependencies to be defined when the app starts
up. These dependencies are then available to be injected into other class
constructors.
